  "environment_caveats": [
    "Live origin: clients/flood-fixers.json records apex cutover as top-level cut_over_at=2026-07-04T20:30:00Z rather than apex_cutover.completed_at. Treated as cut over: the apex https://flood-fixers.com is live (HTTP 200, no x-robots-tag, build_status pushed_main) and both prior audits ran against it. The staging preview still returns x-robots-tag: noindex, as expected, and was not audited.",
    "The DataForSEO MCP wrapper in this CI run exposes only the generic api_request tool (no on_page_lighthouse / on_page_instant_pages wrappers). The audit called the identical REST endpoints (on_page/lighthouse/live/json with for_mobile=false, on_page/instant_pages with enable_javascript, load_resources and validate_micromarkup) using the DATAFORSEO_USERNAME/PASSWORD credentials.",
    "Lighthouse ran DESKTOP only (formFactor=desktop, verified in configSettings). Mobile performance would typically score 10-20 points lower. Scores are not mobile-first.",
    "Micromarkup: instant_pages returned has_micromarkup_errors=true on the 5 pages that carry FAQPage (all except home). A 1-page on_page crawl task with microdata validation showed the only 'error' level results are \"missing field 'answerCount'\" on each FAQPage Question (plus warning \"missing field 'text'\"). answerCount is a QAPage property and is not required by Google's FAQPage structured-data spec, so these are recorded as low severity and do not affect the verdict. JSON-LD on all 6 pages parses cleanly. Info-level findings are real hygiene gaps: LocalBusiness/Organization emit email:\"\", foundingDate:\"\", address.streetAddress:\"\", address.postalCode:\"\", and image/logo as relative paths (/images/logo.webp).",
    "This run enabled validate_micromarkup on instant_pages; last month's run did not surface micromarkup errors, so has_micromarkup_errors is newly surfaced, not necessarily newly broken.",
    "TBT_ms is 0 on all 6 pages. INP_ms is null on all 6 because lab Lighthouse does not emit interaction-to-next-paint.",
    "Broken-link detection: on_page/instant_pages audits a single URL and does not crawl outbound links, so link-level 4xx/5xx checks were not performed. All 6 audited URLs returned 200. No http:// resources found on any page (no mixed content). Image alt coverage is 100% on all 6 pages.",
    "LCP regressions (+321 to +488ms on 4 pages) all remain well inside the 2.5s 'good' threshold. Lab variance between single desktop runs is in the 100-300ms range; the consistent cause across pages this month is the newly added GA4 gtag.js (159KB) which competes for bandwidth during load.",
    "Unweighted/agentic Lighthouse audits (agent-accessibility-tree in the agentic-browsing category) are excluded from lighthouse_issues. It fails on all 6 URLs with the same root cause as link-name.",
    "no_image_title (instant_pages) is not part of the audit rubric and is not recorded as an issue."
  ],
